// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// kind: positive
// expect: ok
//
// ---------- Full silent-bug audit (2026-09-21), area 1 continued +
// arithmetic: bugs in how an earlier implementation represented
// i128/u128, and a broad literal-expected-type
// propagation gap.
// That implementation computed i128's bounds as `(1 << 127) - 1` and
// `-(1 << 127)` in a 128-bit signed integer of its own -- an
// overflow (the bit pattern 1 << 127 is the minimum itself) that
// happened to wrap to the mathematically correct answer in an
// optimised build but was a confirmed crash ("attempt to subtract
// with overflow") in an unoptimised one, where i128 was unusable.
// The crash could only be seen in the unoptimised build, which the
// tests did not use, so this case instead exercises the exact
// arithmetic operations that flowed through the buggy computation
// and checks they are *correct*, not just that nothing crashes;
// the crash itself was confirmed by hand before the fix, not
// re-derived here.

import std;
fn main()
{
    if (!(170141183460469231731687303715884105727: i128 == 170141183460469231731687303715884105727))
    {
        1 /(1 - 1);
    }
}
